fact WorkItem(id: "WI-904", description: some(value: "`typing::is_macro` materializes a full OpInfoRecord to answer a two-field boolean, on a path that runs per fired [simp] rewrite. Surfaced by WI-902's review; PRE-EXISTING since WI-722, which is why it is its own ticket rather than folded into that delivery.\n\nis_macro (kb/typing.rs) -> lookup_operation_info_full -> op_info::lookup_operation_info -> op_info_from_signature (kb/op_info.rs), which CLONES all six per-field signature vectors -- params, return_type, effects, type_params, requires, ensures -- of which is_macro reads exactly `params` and `return_type` (and lookup_operation_info_full drops `ensures`/`meta`/`body_node` immediately). VERIFIED by reading the chain.\n\nTWO COSTS. (a) Operation head: 1-5 Vec alloc/free pairs plus N Value clones per call, to decide a boolean. (b) Non-operation head: `kb.op_record` misses, so lookup_operation_info falls to the linear scan over every anthill.reflect.OperationInfo fact (271 `operation` declarations in stdlib alone, before prelude/builtins) and returns None -- reachable because substitute_to_occurrence builds EVERY functor RHS as an Expr::Apply, so a [simp] rule whose RHS head is an ENTITY CONSTRUCTOR (`rule f(?x) = some(?x) [simp]`) takes the O(N_ops) branch on every fire. Review measured/derived (b); confirm the constructor case by driving before fixing.\n\nSecond-order: try_expand_macro's own doc (kb/simp_rewrite.rs) claims it gates on is_macro \"BEFORE building the argument vector ... so the common path allocates nothing\". The first two conjuncts (as_expr, named/type-args empty) are free; is_macro is not, so the sentence is FALSE as written. Fix the comment with the code.\n\nTHE FIX HAS TWO ESTABLISHED PRECEDENTS in the same module, both introduced for this exact reason: op_info::operation_is_declared (WI-818) and op_info::declared_arity (WI-886), whose doc says \"reading one number should not build an OpInfoRecord, whose construction clones every per-field Vec to be dropped immediately\". Add the third sibling -- e.g. op_info::is_occurrence_signature(kb, op) -> bool -- reading kb.op_record(op).and_then(|r| r.signature.as_ref()) and testing is_occurrence_type over return_type/params BY REFERENCE. Zero-alloc, and it also kills cost (b): a symbol with no record is not an operation, hence not a macro. MIRROR THE TWO TIERS of lookup_operation_info exactly (WI-656 cached record, then the pre-build_op_signatures fact scan) so the classifier's verdict cannot change -- a semantic change here silently turns macros on or off.\n\nSTRONGER OPTION, if measurement justifies it: macro classification is load-stable (OpSignature's own doc: \"the typer rewrites bodies, never signatures, so a cached copy never goes stale within a load\"), so the macro set could be precomputed in build_op_signatures and is_macro become an O(1) set hit at all four call sites, with a KB containing no macros paying one emptiness check.\n\nACCEPTANCE: is_macro answers without constructing an OpInfoRecord and without the O(N_ops) scan for a non-operation head, with the two-tier verdict preserved (a test pinning is_macro's answer for an operation, a constructor, and an unknown symbol, before and after); try_expand_macro's \"allocates nothing\" comment states what the code does; wi722/wi757/wi902 macro suites stay green; cargo-test green via scripts/test.sh."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Open)
